Write the test attempt of FR-GREET-01 for the scenario "A person is greeted by name".

The FR, from the spec:
#### FR-GREET-01: Greet a person by name
`greet(name)` returns a greeting with the person's name. *Why:* people like to be called by their name.

The scenario's steps:
When I greet "Ada"
Then I get "Hello, Ada!"

The scenario fails at the step "I greet "Ada"":
Error [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find module '{tmp}/.oid-worktrees/{project}/{run}/src/greet.ts' imported from {tmp}/.oid-worktrees/{project}/{run}/features/steps/greet.steps.ts
Its step is defined at features/steps/greet.steps.ts:8:
When("I greet {string}", async function (this: GreetWorld, name: string) {
  // A dynamic import, so that a missing module fails this step and not the whole load.
  const { greet } = await import("../../src/greet.ts");
  this.greeting = greet(name);
})

The code relevant to the scenario: the step definitions, the modules they import, and the unit tests that import those.
--- features/steps/greet.steps.ts
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { Then, When } from "@cucumber/cucumber";

interface GreetWorld {
  greeting?: string;
}

When("I greet {string}", async function (this: GreetWorld, name: string) {
  // A dynamic import, so that a missing module fails this step and not the whole load.
  const { greet } = await import("../../src/greet.ts");
  this.greeting = greet(name);
});

Then("I get {string}", function (this: GreetWorld, expected: string) {
  assert.equal(this.greeting, expected);
});

